Analysis of Results 
1. Total Population and Principal Demographic Characteristics
1.1 Total Population  
Total population of Macao comprises local population as well as non-resident workers and non-local 
s
tudents living in Macao. Total population was 682,070 in August 2021, an increase of 129,567 or 23.5% 
compared to August 2011. The average annual growth over the past ten years was 2.1%, a slowdown of 0.3 
percentage points from the 2.4% growth during 2001-2011. 
Chart 1: Population Change 
Non-resident workers and non-local students living in Macao rose by 51.9% and 279.7% respectively 
compared to 2011, with their respective proportions in the total population growing by 2.6 percentage points 
and 1.9 percentage points to 13.9% and 2.8%. Besides, the local population showed an increase of 17.2% over 
the past decade; yet, its proportion in the total population dropped by 4.4 percentage points to 83.4% as the 
growth of the local population was smaller than the increases in non-resident workers and non-local students 
living in Macao. 
Marine population totalled 777, up slightly by 42 compared to 2011. The marine population was mainly 
made up of non-resident workers working on vessels. 
