1.8  Migration Flows
The land-based local population aged 5 and above was 535,931, and 32.8% (175,593) of them had
changed re
sidence in the past five years, up by 1.8 percentage points from 31.0% in 2011. Among those who
had changed residence, 81.8% moved home within Macao (internal migration) and 18.2% moved to Macao
from other places (migration inflow).
The land-based local population who had migrated internally totalled 143,688, an uplift of 53.3% over
2011. Among them, 103,020 moved home within the Macao Peninsula, up by 30,463 (or +42.0%); those who
moved from the Macao Peninsula to “Taipa” or “Coloane” surged by 10,843 to 20,949, more than double
(+107.3%) the figure in 2011.
