1.9  Place of Previous Residence and Length of Residence in Macao
Land-based local population born outside Macao totalled 287,200, up by 28,556 over 2011. Analysed by
place of previous residence, 83.9% (240,893) of them came from mainland China. Among them, 42.8% have
lived in Macao for 30-49 years and most of them were the incoming migrants who moved to the territory
after the reform and opening-up of mainland China; 31.3% have lived in Macao for 5-19 years and the majority
of them moved to the territory by property investment immigration or family reunion reason.
Population with previous place of residence in Hong Kong Special Administrative Region accounted
for 7.7% (22,151). Meanwhile, those with previous place of residence in Myanmar and Cambodia totalled
3,867 and 932 respectively; 85.5% and 93.7% of the respective populations have lived in Macao for 40
years or more, and the majority were the Overseas Chinese in Southeast Asia who moved to Macao during
the 1960’s-1970’s.
