As shown in Chart 18 which illustrates the age structure by statistical district, the youth population (aged
0-14) took up major shares of the populations in “NATAP” (18.9%), “Baixa da Taipa” (18.5%) and “Móng Há &
Reservatório” (17.3%). On the other hand, the districts with relatively high proportions of the elderly
population (aged 65 and above) were “Praia Grande & Penha” (18.4%), “Conselheiro Ferreira de Almeida”
(17.1%) and “Horta e Costa & Ouvidor Arriaga” (15.9%). Among the statistical districts, the top three districts
with the highest median age were “Praia Grande & Penha”(44.1 years), “Conselheiro Ferreira de
Almeida”(43.5 years) and “Jardins do Oceano & Taipa Pequena” (42.9 years).
