2. Economic Activity Status
2.1  Labour Force
Labour force (economically active population) aged 16 and above increased by 8.8% to 377,071,
attri
butable to rising numbers of incoming migrants and non-resident workers in the past ten years; number
of females in the labour force went up by 14.6%, higher than the 3.3% growth in that of males.
