T
he labour market was impacted by population ageing and the pandemic of novel coronavirus
pneumonia. The labour force participation rate fell by 6.9 percentage points from ten years ago to 65.3%. The
respective rates for males and females were 68.7% and 62.4%, down by 9.0 percentage points and 4.8
percentage points respectively; the difference in the labour force participation rates for males and females
narrowed from 10.5 percentage points in 2011 to 6.3 percentage points. The median age of the labour force
rose from 39.1 in 2011 to 40.3.
When excluding non-resident workers and non-local students living in Macao, local labour force totalled
283,396, with males and females accounting for 48.7% and 51.3% respectively. Labour force participation
rate of the local population was 61.1%, with the respective rates for males and females standing at 64.8% and
57.9%. The median age of the local labour force was 41.6, an increase of 0.8 over 2011.
